# Query

Reads and mutations: `apps/web/src/client/shared/queries/use-{verb}.ts`, calling `orpcQuery`.

Reads use `useSuspenseQuery`. The `Suspense` fallback is `Component.Fallback` (or `app/loading.tsx`); no `isLoading` branch beside a suspense query.

```ts
export function useFindOnboarding() {
  return useSuspenseQuery(orpcQuery.organization.findOnboarding.queryOptions());
}
```

```ts
export function useCreateOrganization() {
  return useMutation(orpcQuery.organization.createOrganization.mutationOptions());
}
```

## Resource, not a field

Call the aggregate endpoint and read the field. No `useFindOrganizationName` for a screen that needs the name.

```ts
const { data: organizations } = useFindOrganizations();
const name = organizations[0]?.name;
```

## Paginated lists

`useSuspenseQuery` has no `enabled` and no previous-page placeholder, so paginated lists use `useQuery`.

```ts
export function useFindIssues(input: { cursor?: string }) {
  return useQuery({
    ...orpcQuery.issue.findIssues.queryOptions({ input }),
    placeholderData: keepPreviousData,
  });
}
```
